# Documentation

Entry point to the **{{PROJECT_NAME}}** knowledge base. Every workspace has one owner,
who keeps it current and reviews changes to it
([conventions/ownership.md](../conventions/ownership.md)).

## Project workspaces

The areas every project has, whatever it is built with.

| Workspace | Holds | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Baseline](baseline/README.md) | What the project is held to: scope, assumptions, risks, non-functional requirements. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
| [Architecture](architecture/README.md) | Current and target system shape, platform baseline, cross-repository concerns. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
| [Product](product/README.md) | What is being built and why: requirements, epics and stories as source content. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
| [Delivery](delivery/README.md) | How the project is run: timeline, process, Definition of Ready and Done, sign-off. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
| [Quality](quality/README.md) | How quality is assured: test strategy, checklists, environments, acceptance. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |

## Layer workspaces

One per delivery layer. Each owns its own conventions and contributes decisions under
its `Scope`.

| Workspace | Holds | Owner |
| --- | --- | --- |
| [Backend](backend/README.md) | Server-side services: module layout, API contracts, data model, background work. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
| [Frontend](frontend/README.md) | Browser applications: component and state conventions, routing, design-system usage. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
| [Design](design/README.md) | Design ownership and handoff: who designs, who approves, what a package contains. | {{OWNER_NAME}} |
{{OPTIONAL_LAYER_ROWS}}

## Supporting

| File | Holds |
| --- | --- |
| [decisions/](decisions/README.md) | Every decision record, one folder, with a `Scope` column. Only `Accepted` binds. |
| [glossary.md](glossary.md) | Canonical project vocabulary. |

A layer this project does not have yet — or an area none of the rows above covers —
becomes a workspace when it has content: folder, `README.md`, `CLAUDE.md` with an
owner, and a row above. With the shared plugin installed,
`/{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-shared:{{PROJECT_SLUG}}-space` does all four in one change.
